HST Office: HST Sheets dynamic arrays like the leading spreadsheet application, the hooks in LibreOffice
files (owner 18/11: mandatory in 1.0.3). The behaviour lives in HST-owned files of
hst-sheets-dynamic-array-engine.patch, written from a behaviour spec; this patch only adds the calls.

- Any formula whose result is an array of more than one cell spills when typed (not only an outermost
  array function), as a dynamic array that follows its result's size; a range selection keeps
  Ctrl+Shift+Enter's legacy array. The spill range is not left selected; the input line shows the
  formula without braces; an array formula in the way gives #SPILL! instead of an error dialog
  (viewfunc.cxx, viewfunc.hxx, tabvwsha.cxx call sc::hst helpers).
- A1#, the spill range operator: new opcode ocAnchorArray (ANCHORARRAY, .xlsx _xlfn.ANCHORARRAY, ODF
  COM.MICROSOFT.ANCHORARRAY), parsed by ScCompiler members, evaluated by ScInterpreter::ScAnchorArray,
  shown as A1# by formula::HstFormulaStringWriter (friend of FormulaCompiler). Parameter class
  Reference; it disables threaded group calculation.
- @: implicit intersection with a range (ScInterpreter::ScHstSingleValue, parameter class Reference);
  .xlsx writes it as _xlfn.SINGLE(...) and reads both forms.
- .xlsx: an array formula with cm (dynamic array metadata) is imported as a dynamic array; every
  dynamic array is exported with cm and xl/metadata.xml, not only those calling UNIQUE/SORT/FILTER.

Interface headers: formula/inc/hstformulastrings.hxx, sc/source/ui/inc/hstdynamicarrayinput.hxx
(SPDX LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary). Spec: /data/hst-agents/sheets-103/cleanroom/spec-dynamic-arrays.md.
Test: CppunitTest_sc_hst_dynamic_arrays (with the engine patch).
